    {
      "id": "adjacent_3",
      "question": "What is Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF), and how was it used to train InstructGPT?",
      "category": "out_of_corpus",
      "subtype": "adjacent",
      "top1_score": 0.4159739017486572,
      "abstained": false,
      "response": "Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF) is a training framework that combines human preference data with reinforcement learning to align language models with human values. In the case of InstructGPT, RLHF was used to train the model to follow instructions more effectively by modeling human preferences over model outputs, resulting in responses that are more helpful, accurate, and aligned with user intent. The process typically involves three stages: supervised fine-tuning on demonstration data, reward modeling from human preference judgments, and policy optimization using proximal policy optimization (PPO) to maximize the reward model's scores.\n\nSources:\n- Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Large Language Models: A Survey",
